WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.988
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.474 --> 00:00:09.462
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:22.523 --> 00:00:23.440
RETO MEIER: Hi, there.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.650
And thanks for joining us.

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:25.440
I'm Reto Meier.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:27.065
STEPHANIE WONG: And
I'm Stephanie Wong.

00:00:27.065 --> 00:00:29.530
Many of us are reaching for
hybrid cloud nirvana, which

00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:32.049
makes the workplace mobility
between on-premise and cloud

00:00:32.049 --> 00:00:33.765
computing ideal for our work.

00:00:33.765 --> 00:00:35.140
To help us navigate
through this,

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:37.330
we welcome Chen Goldberg,
Engineering Director

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:38.290
for Google Cloud.

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:39.320
Nice to have you here.

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:39.520
CHEN GOLDBERG: Hi.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:40.930
Thank you very much
for inviting me.

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:41.888
RETO MEIER: Absolutely.

00:00:41.888 --> 00:00:43.570
Now hybrid cloud is
a common strategy

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:45.340
that businesses
look to modernize,

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:47.920
while still supporting
their current applications.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:50.740
How does Google Cloud approach
this particular charge?

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:52.240
CHEN GOLDBERG: So
first of all, it's

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:54.550
important to understand why
customers want to modernize

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:56.437
and why they are
looking for that.

00:00:56.437 --> 00:00:59.020
And the most important thing is
for them, in order to compete,

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:01.360
they have to increase
their developer agility

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:02.957
and help them to
be more focused.

00:01:02.957 --> 00:01:04.540
And they really want
to take advantage

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:07.660
of the amazing capabilities
that are available in the cloud

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:09.593
and using new cloud services.

00:01:09.593 --> 00:01:12.010
But they have to make a decision
and a choice because they

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:15.072
cannot modernize
everything at once.

00:01:15.072 --> 00:01:16.280
That's one of their concerns.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:17.697
The second thing
is that they also

00:01:17.697 --> 00:01:20.080
have concerns from
regulations that requires

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:21.640
them to stay on premises.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:24.100
So from their perspective,
it is a reality

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:26.170
that hybrid is here
to stay and they

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:28.680
have to choose a hybrid
strategy in order

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:31.990
to modernize and
advance their business.

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:33.830
For us at Google
Cloud, we understand

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:36.710
that we need to support our
customers in their journey.

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:37.210
OK?

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:39.310
And our goal is to
make sure that we

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:41.500
help them reduce
the risk, instead

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.990
of increasing the risk when
going through this journey.

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:46.430
And risk are coming
in different levels.

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:50.800
For example, not
fragmenting your talent

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:52.750
and allowing to create
a consistent experience

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:56.620
everywhere, and also really
leveraging the existing assets

00:01:56.620 --> 00:01:57.550
you have today.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.640
So not asking them to buy
new hardware, for example,

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:03.403
but really blending in to
their existing environment.

00:02:03.403 --> 00:02:05.320
STEPHANIE WONG: And how
does this truly differ

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:07.240
from other hybrid offerings?

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:10.840
CHEN GOLDBERG: Google puts the
user at first, in the center.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:13.840
And we understand
that our customers

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:16.330
appreciate to have choice.

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:18.220
They want to be able
to choose where they're

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:21.280
going to deploy their workloads,
what kind of tools, resources

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:22.240
to use.

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:26.680
And our goal is to make that
possible, while reducing risk.

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:30.460
We do it by building our
platform based on open source

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:35.390
technologies, which are ensuring
that their work is portable

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:37.180
and we are not locking them in.

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:41.680
And we're also now approaching
multi-cloud strategically

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:44.950
and giving consistent experience
wherever customers choose

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:46.060
to deploy their workloads.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:46.768
RETO MEIER: Yeah.

00:02:46.768 --> 00:02:47.500
That's amazing.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.630
What components make up Anthos?

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:51.940
And how do those
components work together

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:54.970
to provide a really integrated
approach for our customers?

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:58.420
CHEN GOLDBERG: So Anthos
is a premiere platform

00:02:58.420 --> 00:02:59.758
managed by Google.

00:02:59.758 --> 00:03:01.300
In the foundation,
in the core of it,

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.010
we are using open
source technologies

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:07.750
originated by Google, like
Kubernetes, Istio, and Knative.

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:09.910
But this is not sufficient
for our customer

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:12.610
to manage their trigenious
environments they have.

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:17.140
On top of that, we are building
a multi-cloud, multi-cluster

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:19.870
control plane that lets
our customers connect

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:23.680
to all of their environments
and manage them in a [INAUDIBLE]

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:25.210
through a single pane of glass.

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:28.300
We also give them tools to
manage policies and control

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:30.520
in all of those environments.

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:32.110
But not everything
is containerized.

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:36.170
And this is also about investing
with what they have today.

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:39.850
So on top of that, we are
creating a service management

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:42.790
platform, which allows them
to connect all those services,

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:45.550
regardless of what
compute there is.

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:47.950
And on top of everything we
have an awesome marketplace

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:50.620
that allows us to
provide, both first party

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:53.530
and third party applications
available in all

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:55.040
of those environments.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:55.630
STEPHANIE WONG: So
you just mentioned

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:58.000
investing in what our customers
are already using today.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.387
How can Anthos be used to
help them modernize in place?

00:04:00.387 --> 00:04:02.470
CHEN GOLDBERG: So what we
hear from our customers,

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:06.230
that when they come and they
want to use new cloud services,

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:09.490
they have first to qualify and
make sure that the cloud meets

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:10.600
their bar, right?

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:13.300
Let's say they want to
use BigQuery or even GKE,

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:15.850
they need to go through the
specific process, usually

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:18.370
manual process, to
make sure they can

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:20.200
let their developers use it.

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:23.170
With GKE On-Prem they don't
need to go through that process

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:26.020
because we bring this technology
into their data center

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:28.060
and they know it meets the bar.

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:30.678
So that's actually the fastest
way for them to innovate.

00:04:30.678 --> 00:04:31.720
RETO MEIER: That's great.

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:34.090
What about conflict
management with Anthos?

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:37.330
How can you write multi-cluster
policies right out of the box?

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:39.080
CHEN GOLDBERG: So
that's a great question.

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:41.980
I think that the number
one concern that CEOs have

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:45.170
is how they manage risk
and, specifically, how can

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:47.080
they make sure
that they know who

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:49.240
access what resources
and making sure

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:52.400
that they know what policies
are applied everywhere.

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:54.470
And when you have more
and more environments

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:56.110
you have to build
more and more tools

00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:57.650
and have more
people manage that.

00:04:57.650 --> 00:05:00.310
So Anthos Config
Management allows

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:03.440
you to manage those policies
from a centralized place.

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:05.890
And even if by accident
or by a malicious user,

00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:08.050
someone is trying to
break that policy,

00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:10.690
automatically we will
apply that policy

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:13.780
and bring that environment
back to be compliant.

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:14.570
RETO MEIER: Great.

00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:16.270
STEPHANIE WONG: So more
environments, more tools.

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:17.860
Can you elaborate
on what we're doing

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:19.678
to users the
visibility they need,

00:05:19.678 --> 00:05:21.220
so that they can
see what's happening

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:22.780
across all these environments?

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:23.572
CHEN GOLDBERG: Yes.

00:05:23.572 --> 00:05:25.840
So we are leveraging
open APIs, which

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:28.180
allows us to actually integrate
with every environment,

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:30.070
wherever the user chooses.

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:32.380
And we are creating
tools, centralized tools,

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:35.860
in the control plane that
gives you signals or monitoring

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:37.390
data from all of
those environments

00:05:37.390 --> 00:05:39.120
in a consistent way.

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:41.440
And we're also leveraging
things like Knative.

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:43.810
We just announced
Cloud Run as beta

00:05:43.810 --> 00:05:47.590
to give a simple and effective
user experience for developers,

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:49.840
again to deploy to all
of those environments.

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:51.430
So when I think
about it, it's not

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:53.740
about portability of
workloads, but it's actually

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:55.720
about portability of skills.

00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:58.630
Can my developers, can
my service operators

00:05:58.630 --> 00:06:02.092
use the same set of tools,
regardless of which environment

00:06:02.092 --> 00:06:02.800
they want to use?

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:05.030
And by leveraging open
source technologies,

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:06.113
this is actually possible.

00:06:06.113 --> 00:06:06.822
RETO MEIER: Yeah.

00:06:06.822 --> 00:06:07.780
That's fantastic.

00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:10.990
I'm curious, how are
customers using Anthos today?

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:13.180
And what are some of the
more interesting use cases

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:14.680
that you may have come across?

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:17.470
CHEN GOLDBERG: I'm smiling
because, ever since we've

00:06:17.470 --> 00:06:21.550
announced back that it was
CSP eight months ago as alpha,

00:06:21.550 --> 00:06:26.050
we've seen an overwhelming
excitement with our customers.

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:29.560
Over 1,000 customers showed
interest, just during Next,

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:33.820
to try out CSV Anthos.

00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:37.370
And we see a different
type of use cases.

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:39.670
So I would say for
someone like HSBC,

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:43.180
they were excited to give
their developers platform,

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:45.520
a modern platform,
without having

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:49.110
to go through all
the qualification

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:51.620
and making sure that the new
environment meets the bar.

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:52.810
So they're doing both.

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:54.727
But they know that for
some of their workloads

00:06:54.727 --> 00:06:56.670
they will have to stay On-Prem.

00:06:56.670 --> 00:06:59.210
And we see other customers,
like Kohl's for example,

00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:01.960
that are looking to
innovate, both On-Prem

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:04.870
and in the cloud and create
a consistent environment.

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:09.230
And maybe talking about
a customer like KeyBank.

00:07:09.230 --> 00:07:09.730
OK?

00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:12.015
So they're really excited
about the agility.

00:07:12.015 --> 00:07:14.140
So really leveraging new
tools and making sure they

00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:16.300
can deploy quickly in
other environments.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:19.870
So different customers
see different use cases

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:22.750
to begin with, but they're all
very excited, by both agility

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:23.543
and reducing risk.

00:07:23.543 --> 00:07:25.210
RETO MEIER: Thanks,
Chen, for walking us

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:27.020
through the
possibilities of Anthos.

00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:27.880
CHEN GOLDBERG: Thank
you for having me.

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:28.797
RETO MEIER: Of course.

00:07:28.797 --> 00:07:31.230
